WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.730 --> 00:00:03.140
Where's Bobby?

00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:05.420
I got to let her know the
real killer has to be Crass.

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:06.380
[CRASH]

00:00:06.380 --> 00:00:07.340
[GASPS]

00:00:07.340 --> 00:00:10.700
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:16.470 --> 00:00:17.580
Sorry I'm late.

00:00:17.580 --> 00:00:26.000
I hope there aren't
any objections.

00:00:26.000 --> 00:00:27.920
Your honor, may I
approach the bench?

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.140
I wish you would.

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:31.460
Watch this kid.

00:00:31.460 --> 00:00:34.292
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:50.460
(SINGING) If it pleases the
court-- and I know that I do--

00:00:50.460 --> 00:00:55.540
there's something that
I simply must address.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:57.100
I have heard a report--

00:00:57.100 --> 00:01:00.040
and I swear it's not true--

00:01:00.040 --> 00:01:04.720
about the secret to
my great success.

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:10.110
So I am here to set
the record straight.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:15.720
There are just two methods
that I use to help me litigate.

00:01:18.780 --> 00:01:25.630
Bells and whistles will get
'em all, although the purest,

00:01:25.630 --> 00:01:27.250
they may scoff.

00:01:27.250 --> 00:01:33.590
All you need are bells and
whistles to win the case,

00:01:33.590 --> 00:01:37.910
though other jurists may
say, you're a disgrace.

00:01:37.910 --> 00:01:40.940
The prosecution-- they
may rest, convinced

00:01:40.940 --> 00:01:42.590
that they have done their best.

00:01:42.590 --> 00:01:44.120
Then I've stopped blowing.

00:01:44.120 --> 00:01:45.380
I've stopped clanging.

00:01:45.380 --> 00:01:47.720
One more Joe avoids a hanging.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:52.250
Bells and whistles
are all you need,

00:01:52.250 --> 00:01:57.366
plus a comprehensive
knowledge of the law.

00:01:57.366 --> 00:02:00.360
[TAPPING]

00:02:06.847 --> 00:02:09.342
[SAXOPHONE PLAYING]

00:02:09.342 --> 00:02:12.336
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:27.320 --> 00:02:30.518
(SINGING) Plus a comprehensive
knowledge of the--

00:02:30.518 --> 00:02:32.810
thank you to the judge and
all the members of the jury.

00:02:32.810 --> 00:02:34.100
I will try to make
this brief, because I

00:02:34.100 --> 00:02:34.790
know you're in a hurry.

00:02:34.790 --> 00:02:35.810
See, my client-- the defendant--

00:02:35.810 --> 00:02:37.760
Dr. Joshua de Skinner--
he was merely at the club

00:02:37.760 --> 00:02:38.960
to take his darling
wife to dinner.

00:02:38.960 --> 00:02:40.850
He stumbled on the body of
Miss Chelsea-- the decedent.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:41.870
And you may jump to conclusions.

00:02:41.870 --> 00:02:42.920
But the fact is
that you needn't.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.780
The prima facie evidence--
oh, it's an avalanche--

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:46.070
will be expressly
and indubitably

00:02:46.070 --> 00:02:47.000
proven circumstantial.

00:02:47.000 --> 00:02:47.960
The testimony is hearsay.

00:02:47.960 --> 00:02:48.950
And it reeks of retribution.

00:02:48.950 --> 00:02:51.367
So what we have here is nothing
but malicious prosecution.

00:02:51.367 --> 00:02:53.720
And a verdict of not guilty
is the only just solution.

00:02:53.720 --> 00:02:57.450
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:02:57.450 --> 00:03:01.920
(SINGING) Bells and
whistles are all you need,

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.750
plus a comprehensive knowledge--
the kind you get in college--

00:03:06.750 --> 00:03:12.070
a comprehensive
knowledge of the law.

00:03:16.720 --> 00:03:19.780
I certainly hope this
won't be a split decision.

00:03:19.780 --> 00:03:22.830
[CLAPPING]

